## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Evidence sourcing approach:** Should I manually extract reference figures from the Shell/Tata Power/Microsoft PDFs that are already on disk, or should I build the `build_evidence_corpus.py` script first and use a semi-automated approach? Manual is faster but doesn't scale; scripted takes longer but is reusable.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 2. **70B re-extraction cost:** Re-extracting all 6 reports through NVIDIA 70B will consume API credits. The existing claims are cached — should I re-extract only the 3 reports with known mislabels (Shell 2022/2023, Tata Power) or all 6?

> [!WARNING]
> 3. **Docker + local Postgres:** The current system uses hosted Supabase. Adding a local Postgres in docker-compose creates a dual-DB setup. Should the Dockerfile target Supabase-only (simpler, production-first) or include a local PG option (more self-contained, better for dev)?

> [!NOTE]
> 4. **Gold set labeling:** Creating 100 gold-labeled claims requires reading the source PDFs and manually verifying each claim's fields. This is ~2–3 hours of focused work. Is this acceptable, or should I start with a smaller seed (30 claims) and expand iteratively?
